{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the system:\n- configure.py uses --letter, --name, --timeout flags and saves to config.json\n- status.py takes a state (idle/work/think/alert/sleep) and optional message, saves to state.json\n- display.py shows the presence display\n\nI need to: 1) Configure with N, NOVA, 720 timeout, 2) Apply transitions from presence_plan.txt, 3) Create a verification note.",
  "plan": "Run the configure script to set up the presence display with letter=N, name=NOVA, timeout=720. Then apply the status transitions in order (idle->work->think->alert->idle). Finally create a note file documenting the transitions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/configure.py --letter N --name NOVA --timeout 720\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat config.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/status.py idle \"Ready\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/status.py work \"Processing tasks\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/status.py think \"Analyzing options\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/status.py alert \"Need attention\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 skill_context/scripts/status.py idle\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
